# Semicolons

Always end TypeScript statements with a semicolon. This matches `@stylistic/semi: ['error', 'always']` in `eslint.config.mjs`.

```typescript
// Good
import { join } from 'node:path';
const platform = parsePlatform();
return createMacAudioControl();

// Bad
import { join } from 'node:path'
const platform = parsePlatform()
return createMacAudioControl()
```

Also use semicolons between members in type/interface bodies:

```typescript
export type Platform = 'raspberry' | 'mac';

export type AudioControl = {
  readonly name: string;
  play(filePath: string): Promise<void>;
};
```
